而且等我不得不放弃的时候，我会大吵大闹、拼死抵抗的。

210
00:09:15.870 --> 00:09:16.630
That's right.
没毛病。

211
00:09:16.630 --> 00:09:23.630
Here are some reasons, not related to a zombie apocalypse, where you might want a landline.
以下是一些与僵尸末日无关、你可能想要一部座机的原因。

212
00:09:23.830 --> 00:09:28.910
I know I often talk about the zombie apocalypse as my reason for needing these services.
我知道我经常把僵尸末日当作我需要这些服务的原因。

213
00:09:29.190 --> 00:09:30.770
But there's other reasons.
但还有其他原因。

214
00:09:30.930 --> 00:09:31.250
Okay.
好吧。

215
00:09:31.710 --> 00:09:35.450
If there's a power outage from a flood, a fire, or other natural disaster.
如果发生洪水、火灾或其他自然灾害导致断电。

216
00:09:35.890 --> 00:09:38.070
Katie Lanza, who was 37.
凯蒂·兰扎（Katie Lanza），当时37岁。

217
00:09:38.550 --> 00:09:39.570
She's from 37.
她来自 37。

218
00:09:39.590 --> 00:09:41.110
We got a young'un in there.
我们这儿来了个年轻人。

219
00:09:41.270 --> 00:09:41.510
Yeah.
是啊。

220
00:09:42.250 --> 00:09:45.810
She's from Fort Worth, and she said that her dog chewed her cell phone.
她来自沃斯堡，她说她的狗把她的手机给啃了。

221
00:09:46.130 --> 00:09:52.610
And while she was waiting to get her replacement, she got sick in the middle of the night, and she needed help, and she didn't have a phone.
就在她等待更换新手机的时候，她在半夜生病了，她需要帮助，而她却没有电话。

222
00:09:52.810 --> 00:09:54.730
She had to go to her neighbor's house to use a phone.
她不得不去邻居家借电话。

223
00:09:54.870 --> 00:09:57.570
And ever since, she's had a true landline.
从那以后，她就装了一条真正的固定电话。

224
00:09:57.970 --> 00:09:58.850
So there you go.
所以你看。

225
00:09:58.970 --> 00:09:59.290
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

226
00:09:59.790 --> 00:10:01.390
Flood, fire, natural disaster.
洪水、火灾、自然灾害。

227
00:10:01.790 --> 00:10:03.270
Something happens to your cell phone.
你的手机出了点状况。

228
00:10:03.650 --> 00:10:04.610
I'm not done.
我还没说完呢。

229
00:10:04.790 --> 00:10:05.190
Okay?
好吗？

230
00:10:05.190 --> 00:10:08.190
I didn't think you were, because you're holding several pieces of paper.
我可没觉得你说完了，因为你手里还拿着好几页纸呢。

231
00:10:08.510 --> 00:10:08.650
Yeah.
对。

232
00:10:09.030 --> 00:10:18.050
Francella Jackson, 61, from Illinois, said she worries about cyber attacks disrupting her cell service, and that's why she has a landline.
来自伊利诺伊州的弗兰塞拉·杰克逊（Francella Jackson），61岁，她说她担心网络攻击会中断她的手机服务，这就是她拥有固定电话的原因。

233
00:10:18.950 --> 00:10:27.610
After I read this article, it compelled me to double-check with my phone company to make sure that they hadn't switched me again, and I do still have a POTS.
在我读了这篇文章后，它迫使我再次跟我的电话公司核实，以确保他们没有悄悄把我换掉，而且我确实还有一个传统老式电话（POTS）。

234
00:10:27.710 --> 00:10:29.610
I do have that copper landline.
我确实有那种铜线座机。

235
00:10:29.690 --> 00:10:30.330
Good for you.
那可真不错。

236
00:10:30.330 --> 00:10:34.350
And we have the cutest little old-timey phone with the little buttons.
而且我们还有一个带小按键的、最可爱的小老式电话。

237
00:10:34.570 --> 00:10:36.850
My kids are mesmerized by it.
我的孩子们对它着迷不已。

238
00:10:37.010 --> 00:10:44.230
They love to call us on our cell phones from the landline and, like, prank us.
他们喜欢用座机拨打我们的手机，然后，就好像是恶作剧一样。

239
00:10:44.530 --> 00:10:45.370
That's cute.
真可爱。

240
00:10:45.550 --> 00:10:46.050
They love it.
他们喜欢得不得了。

241
00:10:46.190 --> 00:10:47.950
Push-button phone, old-timey.
按键式电话，老式的。

242
00:10:48.330 --> 00:10:50.170
